  "final_text": "The dashboard and the alert rule both exist. I didn't open the dashboard or check that the rule actually runs.\n\n**Data:** The logs data view has `timestamp`, `response` (a string, so 404 and 503 are text), `bytes`, `extension`, `geo.src`, `clientip`, `machine.os`, `host`, `url` and `request`.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-38453110 Web logs overview\" has five panels:\n- Total requests\n- Requests over time\n- Requests by response code\n- Average bytes by file extension\n- Top source countries\n\nIt's at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-38453110-web-logs-overview-05c2375e802a.\n\n**Alert rule:** \"EFF-38453110 5xx spike\" is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`.\n- It runs every minute.\n- It looks at the last 5 minutes and fires when more than 10 documents match a regexp on `response.keyword` for `5xx`.\n- It was created disabled, so I enabled it. It now shows as enabled, but it has no action connector, so it won't send notifications when it fires.",
